WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.760
Hey YouTubers. It's Charlie. So this is going to be my Flash episode nineteen video.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.116
Also kind of like a soft cross over with Arrow, just like we had last week.

00:00:08.116 --> 00:00:12.636
I know everyone was playing up the episode eighteen all-star team up episode as the big cross over but

00:00:12.636 --> 00:00:16.378
this was actually really big too for reasons that we'll get into during spoilers.

00:00:16.378 --> 00:00:18.705
So just careful if you haven't seen the episode yet

00:00:18.705 --> 00:00:20.747
and yay for Green Lantern pizza.

00:00:20.747 --> 00:00:23.294
OK so here we go starting with top five WTF moments. 

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.960
Number Five: Cisco gives Laurel her Canary Cry.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.421
One of the biggest questions I've gotten all season is

00:00:29.421 --> 00:00:32.383
will there be another particle accelerator explosion,

00:00:32.383 --> 00:00:35.421
and will Laurel get Canary Cry powers as result of that?

00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:38.151
This is the answer. She's basically using tech.

00:00:38.151 --> 00:00:41.371
If you ever watch Young Justice, you know Canary wears the choker.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.680
Think of this as like a tech version of that.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.980
Cisco explains that this is super beefed up

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.335
so it'll be super bad ass. They'll probably use it before the end of the season.

00:00:49.335 --> 00:00:52.420
Because the episodes are staggered I don't know when we're going to see this

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.569
being used in an episode of Arrow. It might be like

00:00:54.569 --> 00:00:57.490
Arrow episode twenty-two. It might even be like the finale.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.600
The picture that Laurel gave to Cisco is the funniest thing in the world. 

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.817
He's like the biggest

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.540
Black Canary super fan.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.078
Let me know which picture you think is funnier. Cisco's picture with the Black Canary,

00:01:07.078 --> 00:01:08.960
or the picture of Steven Amell

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.917
like the actor head shot they used. The Glamour Shot

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.440
in episode nineteen.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.660
On to number four: meet Hannibal Bates

00:01:15.846 --> 00:01:18.086
a.k.a. Everyman from the comics.

00:01:18.086 --> 00:01:20.412
If you're not familiar with the character, Everyman

00:01:20.412 --> 00:01:23.081
came around the Infinite Crisis time in the comics.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.100
Lex Luthor created a program

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.044
called The Everyman Project

00:01:27.044 --> 00:01:29.980
where he gave powers to people that wanted them.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.335
It was part of his secret plot to control people with super powers like

00:01:33.335 --> 00:01:35.902
he could take away their powers with the push of a button.

00:01:35.902 --> 00:01:38.360
Obviously we're not going to see Lex Luthor on The Flash so

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.515
this is just like The Flash's version of Hannibal Bates.

00:01:41.515 --> 00:01:46.314
It's interesting that he can't remember who he really is. He's changed into so many people.

00:01:46.314 --> 00:01:50.093
Also when Harrison said that it's meant to highlight the balance between

00:01:50.093 --> 00:01:51.720
the original Harrison Wells

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.177
and Eobard Thawne inside that one body.

00:01:54.177 --> 00:01:56.078
The producers said that when the Reverse Flash

00:01:56.347 --> 00:01:58.427
sucked in all of Harrison Wells

00:01:58.427 --> 00:02:01.063
it kind of melded their minds a little bit together so there

00:02:01.063 --> 00:02:04.702
is some of the original Harrison Wells mind inside that body.

00:02:04.702 --> 00:02:08.160
It will probably explain how they can defeat the Reverse Flash at the end of the season but

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.622
Tom Cavanagh doesn't have to leave the show.

00:02:10.622 --> 00:02:12.667
That's going to get really timey-wimey.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:15.696
As a source of villainy Hannibal Bates, not such a

00:02:15.696 --> 00:02:18.428
threatening villain. I think he's better for comedy.

00:02:18.428 --> 00:02:21.267
Like the "snowbarry" kiss for instance, that was a really funny moment,

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:23.640
especially with the music cues they used behind it,

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.052
you knew that it was going to be a funny thing.

00:02:26.052 --> 00:02:30.234
I was actually tweeting during the episode about how it was funny that Danielle Panabaker

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:33.360
didn't have the classic "slap reaction" that you would expect

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.513
like "how dare you kiss me? what's wrong with you?"

00:02:35.513 --> 00:02:40.783
It was a couple minutes after it happened, it was by the time Caitlin had made it back to Barry's house and found him in the closet.

00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:43.520
Cut to her slapping him to wake him up.

00:02:43.521 --> 00:02:45.885
Think of it as like a delayed slap reaction.

00:02:45.885 --> 00:02:50.000
I'm not like a huge shipper on the show but it is funny when they sneak in moments like that.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.000
We do have an idea where Cailtin and Firestorm's characters are going so

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.947
if you've seen those spoilers just please use spoiler tags if you're going to comment on them.

00:02:58.947 --> 00:03:01.982
The real question we need to ask now is will Harrison Wells

00:03:01.997 --> 00:03:06.237
co-opt Hannibal's services in the finale or before the finale? 

00:03:06.237 --> 00:03:10.500
It just seems like he might release a lot of meta-humans to run interference on Team Flash 

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.948
while he's enacting whatever his evil final plan is.

00:03:12.948 --> 00:03:17.519
On to number three: Eddie reveals to Iris that he's been working with The Flash.

00:03:17.519 --> 00:03:21.500
This whole thing with Iris not knowing is causing more problems than it's solving.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.245
That was what that whole car escape scene was about.

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:26.984
Iris demanded they take Hannibal to the police station

00:03:26.984 --> 00:03:29.833
because she didn't understand what a threat he was.

00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:32.260
Eddie telling Iris is just the tip of the iceberg.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.407
He hasn't explained anything yet.

00:03:34.407 --> 00:03:37.666
Iris is aware that meta-humans exist. She just doesn't know the

00:03:37.666 --> 00:03:39.360
full extent of what's going on.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.551
There are four more episodes in the season so I'd say by the next two or three episodes

00:03:43.551 --> 00:03:45.611
she'll have it pretty much figured out.

00:03:45.611 --> 00:03:48.179
That doesn't include finding out that Barry is The Flash though.

00:03:48.179 --> 00:03:50.828
That's probably going to be some other big WTF moment.

00:03:50.828 --> 00:03:55.198
She'll probably figure it out on her own. Barry won't just take his mask off and reveal himself.

00:03:55.198 --> 00:04:00.065
If she's going to be a reporter and the writers want us to take her as a character seriously,

00:04:00.065 --> 00:04:03.908
then logically she should be able to do the detective work to figure out

00:04:03.908 --> 00:04:06.026
that Barry is The Flash on her own.

00:04:06.026 --> 00:04:11.000
When Candice Patton was talking about her character she called out Lois Lane and in Man of Steel

00:04:11.014 --> 00:04:15.094
Lois Lane figured out that Clark Kent was Superman on her own.

00:04:15.094 --> 00:04:16.835
Really early in the movie actually.

00:04:16.835 --> 00:04:21.311
Moving on to number two: Team Flash finds Harrison Wells' original body.

00:04:21.311 --> 00:04:25.698
I like how they bought Quentin into the episode. Like Joe and Quentin have this "dad cop"

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:26.741
bro-out moment.

00:04:26.741 --> 00:04:29.409
"You would do anything to save your daughter if you could."

00:04:29.409 --> 00:04:34.058
Quentin knows something is up. He knows there's a dead body. He knows it's probably Harrison Wells.

00:04:34.058 --> 00:04:37.013
He just doesn't know the full extend of what's going on with the meta-humans,

00:04:37.013 --> 00:04:39.374
and he doesn't know that Barry is The Flash.

00:04:39.374 --> 00:04:42.315
I think he knows that something really weird is going on because

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:44.820
everyone saw his coffee rising out of the cup

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:49.604
but he doesn't have the context to understand what the larger ramifications of it are.

00:04:49.604 --> 00:04:54.104
Showing Caitlin the body too I think won her over. For most of the episode there was a big question as to

00:04:54.104 --> 00:04:57.408
whether or not she was going to try and side with Harrison Wells

00:04:57.429 --> 00:04:58.949
and not believe Barry.

00:04:58.949 --> 00:05:03.019
I think seeing the body was the metaphorical slap in the face that she needed.

00:05:03.019 --> 00:05:05.370
and finally my number one WTF moment:

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.530
Team Flash makes it inside the Gideon computer room,

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.893
and Harrison Wells is inquiring with Eddie Thawne.

00:05:11.893 --> 00:05:14.600
This is like our big endgame moment so Team Flash

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.240
sees the Reverse Flash suit 

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:19.719
and sees the future newspaper "Flash disappears in crisis"

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:21.668
and then over on the other side of town,

00:05:21.668 --> 00:05:25.099
Harrison Wells is slowly moving in on Eddie Thawne.

00:05:25.099 --> 00:05:27.565
So let's start with the Gideon computer room stuff.

00:05:27.565 --> 00:05:29.820
Seeing the yellow suit was a big WTF

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:34.083
but really I think the bigger surprise for them was seeing the newspaper from the future.

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:37.631
They don't know who Eobard Thawne is. They don't know that he's from the future.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:42.260
What I think that crisis might be is The Flash disappearing

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:45.207
because he went back in time to chase The Reverse Flash

00:05:45.207 --> 00:05:46.944
to the night that his mother was murdered.

00:05:46.944 --> 00:05:49.197
That might be what that is originally from.

00:05:49.197 --> 00:05:53.465
Moving over to the police station, what is Eobard Thawne's plan for Eddie Thawne?

00:05:53.465 --> 00:05:56.031
Is he going to try and co-opt his services?

00:05:56.031 --> 00:05:58.100
Eddie, right now, is a good person.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:01.869
He is friends with Barry. Very good friends with Barry and Team Flash.

00:06:01.869 --> 00:06:05.116
That means that The Reverse Flash is going to have to trick

00:06:05.189 --> 00:06:07.349
Eddie or force Eddie to help him.

00:06:07.349 --> 00:06:09.702
Which means he might start going after Iris.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.122
Iris would be the way to do that.

00:06:11.122 --> 00:06:13.376
That's a very classic Reverse Flash thing.

00:06:13.376 --> 00:06:17.347
Threatening to kill the wife or girlfriends of The Flash over the years.

00:06:17.347 --> 00:06:19.874
So with that in mind, here's my big question for you guys.

00:06:19.874 --> 00:06:24.052
What do you think that Eobard Thawne's plan is for Eddie Thawne?

00:06:24.052 --> 00:06:27.211
I think I've said it before but what I think the show is moving towards

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.660
is a big WTF moment

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.146
where by Eddie Thawne will have a falling out with Barry Allen.

00:06:33.146 --> 00:06:34.680
Slowly sowing the seeds

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:37.315
for Eddie to become a villain in a future season. 

00:06:37.315 --> 00:06:39.865
Whether that's season two, season three we have no idea.

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:43.326
There's still a whole bunch of stuff that hasn't happened this season. The Reverse Flash

00:06:43.326 --> 00:06:46.786
still has all these meta-humans that he can unleash on Team Flash,

00:06:46.786 --> 00:06:50.444
including Gorilla Grod. That's not for another two episodes though.

00:06:50.444 --> 00:06:54.942
Next week is called "The Trap" so they're going to try and set a trap for The Reverse Flash.

00:06:54.942 --> 00:06:57.800
Clearly I don't think anyone expects it to go well.

